>
> When forming lujvo, it is possible to extend the literal meaning of
> the components, so even if "se fusra" is limited to bio-catalysts that
> facilitate catabolic reactions, that doesn't mean that "selfusra"
> can't have a wider application. Perhaps "zanfusra" and "malfusra" can
> distinguish the ana- and cata-bolic types.
>

I don't think catabolism should have a derogative sense. It "provides the
chemical energy necessary for the maintenance and growth of cells":
 http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catabolism

We want to consider "metabolic" as well. Again something with "fusra". I
feel that "anabolic" and "catabolic" should be based on that lujvo, not on
"fusra" itself.
 http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metabolism

